### Source 1: Jira Issues — "What happened before?"

* This is from your documentation. Fully implemented.*

#### What It Does

When an alert arrives, InfraAI searches your Jira instance(s) for **past incidents with similar symptoms**. It finds resolved tickets and injects their **resolutions, comments, and workarounds** into the AI prompt.

#### How It Works — Step by Step

    Alert arrives: "ORA-01653 tablespace full USERS_DATA on prod-db-01"
            │
            ▼
    STEP 1: Extract search terms from alert
            Keywords: "ORA-01653", "tablespace", "USERS_DATA", "prod-db-01"
            │
            ▼
    STEP 2: Build JQL query
            project IN (OPS, INFRA, INC)
            AND status IN (Done, Resolved, Closed)
            AND issueType IN (Bug, Incident, Problem)
            AND text ~ "ORA-01653 tablespace"
            │
            ▼
    STEP 3: Execute search via Jira REST API
            GET https://acme.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/search?jql=...
            │
            ▼
    STEP 4: Process results
            Found 3 matching issues:
            • OPS-1234 (Resolved 2025-11-15) — Tablespace full, fixed by adding datafile
            • INC-567 (Resolved 2025-08-22) — Archive logs not purged after patching
            • OPS-890 (Resolved 2025-03-10) — USERS_DATA autoextend disabled
            │
            ▼
    STEP 5: Extract useful data from each issue
            For each issue:
            • Summary and description
            • Resolution comments
            • Fix that was applied
            • Root cause identified
            • Labels and components
            │
            ▼
    STEP 6: Format as AI context
            ## Jira Historical Issues
            
            ### OPS-1234 (Resolved 2025-11-15)
            Summary: Tablespace USERS_DATA full on prod-db-01
            Resolution: Added datafile users_data02.dbf (2GB, autoextend ON).
            Purged archive logs older than 7 days.
            Root cause: Archive log cleanup cron disabled after Oct patching.
            
            ### INC-567 (Resolved 2025-08-22)
            ...

