#### JQL — The Query Language

JQL (Jira Query Language) is how InfraAI searches Jira. Let me explain it simply:

    JQL is like SQL but for Jira issues.

    SQL:   SELECT * FROM issues WHERE project = 'OPS' AND status = 'Resolved'
    JQL:   project = OPS AND status = Resolved

    More examples:

    Find all resolved incidents mentioning tablespace:
      project IN (OPS, INFRA) 
      AND status IN (Resolved, Done) 
      AND issueType = Incident 
      AND text ~ "tablespace"

    Find all critical bugs in the last 90 days:
      project = OPS 
      AND issueType = Bug 
      AND priority = Critical 
      AND resolved >= -90d

    Find issues related to a specific server:
      text ~ "prod-db-01" 
      AND status IN (Resolved, Closed)

#### Security — JQL Injection Prevention

* From your documentation:*

> *"Search queries are derived from alert metadata — no raw user input is sent directly to JQL. JQL special characters are escaped to prevent injection."*

What this means:

    SAFE:
      Alert text: "ORA-01653 tablespace full"
      InfraAI builds JQL: text ~ "ORA-01653 tablespace full"
      Special chars escaped: text ~ "ORA\\-01653 tablespace full"

    PREVENTED:
      If someone crafted a malicious alert payload:
      Alert text: "test\" OR project = SECRET_PROJECT AND text ~ \""
      InfraAI escapes: text ~ "test\\\" OR project \\= SECRET..."
      → Treated as literal search text, not JQL operators
      → Cannot access projects outside the configured scope

