##### Step 5: Search (At Query Time)

When an alert arrives and the system needs knowledge context:

    ALERT: "ORA-01653 tablespace full USERS_DATA"
              │
              ▼
    STEP A: Convert alert text to embedding vector
            "ORA-01653 tablespace full USERS_DATA"
            → [0.234, -0.876, 0.123, ...]
              │
              ▼
    STEP B: Query pgvector for similar chunks
            SELECT content, 
                   1 - (embedding <=> query_vector) AS similarity_score
            FROM knowledge_chunks
            ORDER BY embedding <=> query_vector
            LIMIT 5;  -- top_k = 5 (from rag_top_k setting)
              │
              ▼
    STEP C: Filter by score threshold
            Only keep results with similarity > 0.7 
            (from rag_score_threshold setting)
              │
              ▼
    STEP D: Return ranked results with source attribution
            
            Result 1 (score: 0.94):
              Source: "Oracle Tablespace Management SOP" (SharePoint)
              Chunk: "When ORA-01653 occurs, first check autoextend
                      status. If disabled, add a new datafile..."
            
            Result 2 (score: 0.89):
              Source: "OPS-1234" (Jira, resolved 2025-11-15)
              Chunk: "Root cause: Archive log cleanup cron disabled 
                      after October patching. Fix: re-enable cron,
                      purge logs older than 7 days."
            
            Result 3 (score: 0.82):
              Source: "prod-db-01 Architecture" (GitHub)
              Chunk: "USERS_DATA tablespace: autoextend deliberately
                      disabled per DBA policy to prevent filling /u01."

**The `<=>` operator** is pgvector's **cosine distance** operator. It computes how similar two vectors are. Lower distance = more similar. We convert to similarity score: `1 - distance`.

#### PII Redaction During Ingestion

* From your RAG plan:*

> *"PII redaction: pii\_redactor.py applied during ingestion before embedding. Prevents sensitive data from being stored in vectors."*

    BEFORE PII REDACTION:
      "John Smith (john.smith@acme.com, SSN: 123-45-6789) 
       resolved the tablespace issue on prod-db-01"

    AFTER PII REDACTION:
      "[PERSON] ([EMAIL], SSN: [REDACTED]) resolved the 
       tablespace issue on prod-db-01"

    This happens BEFORE the text is chunked and embedded.
    The vector store never contains raw PII.

**Why this matters:** The embedded chunks are sent to external AI providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.). PII redaction ensures **personal data never leaves your environment** via AI API calls.

