    │                                                               │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

**Content hash is brilliant.** If a document hasn't changed since last sync (same SHA256 hash), it's skipped entirely. No re-chunking, no re-embedding, no cost. This means periodic syncs are **fast and cheap** when most documents haven't changed.

