###  Keyword Search vs Semantic Search — The Dual Approach

InfraAI uses **BOTH** types of search. Here's why:

    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │         KEYWORD SEARCH vs SEMANTIC SEARCH                     │
    │                                                               │
    │  KEYWORD (Jira JQL, Confluence CQL, ServiceNow API)          │
    │  ══════════════════════════════════════════════               │
    │  How: Exact text matching with operators                      │
    │  Query: text ~ "ORA-01653"                                   │
    │  Matches: Documents containing "ORA-01653"                    │
    │  Misses: "tablespace capacity exceeded" (no "ORA-01653")     │
    │                                                               │
    │   Strengths:                                                │
    │  • Perfect for error codes (ORA-01653, ERR-500)              │
    │  • Perfect for exact matches (server names, ticket numbers)  │
    │  • Fast (uses database indexes)                              │
    │  • No AI cost (no embedding needed)                          │
    │                                                               │
    │   Weaknesses:                                               │
    │  • Misses semantically similar content                       │
    │  • Requires exact keywords to match                          │
    │  • Can't understand meaning                                  │
    │                                                               │
    │                                                               │
    │  SEMANTIC (pgvector RAG)                                      │
    │  ═══════════════════════                                     │
    │  How: Vector similarity (cosine distance)                     │
    │  Query: "tablespace full" → vector → compare                 │
    │  Matches: Anything with SIMILAR MEANING                       │
    │  Finds: "storage exhausted", "disk space issue", "ORA-01653" │
    │                                                               │
    │   Strengths:                                                │
    │  • Finds content by meaning, not just words                  │
    │  • Handles synonyms, paraphrases, different languages        │
    │  • Discovers non-obvious connections                         │
    │                                                               │
    │   Weaknesses:                                               │
    │  • Requires embedding (small AI cost)                        │
    │  • Can return false positives (similar but irrelevant)        │
    │  • Requires pgvector setup                                   │
    │                                                               │
    │                                                               │
    │  InfraAI USES BOTH:                                           │
    │  ════════════════                                            │
    │  Jira → Keyword (JQL) — perfect for finding exact tickets    │
    │  Confluence → Keyword (CQL) — perfect for KB article titles  │
    │  ServiceNow → Keyword (API filters) — structured data        │
    │  pgvector → Semantic — catches everything keywords miss       │
    │                                                               │
    │  Together: Maximum recall with minimum noise                  │
    │                                                               │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

